id: pm-web-t03i
title: Add generic self-hostable OIDC login
description: "Add optional provider-neutral OIDC Authorization Code + PKCE login to public pm-web with external identity mapping, secure state handling, UI discovery, docs, and tests."
type: Task
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[5]: auth,oidc,pkce,security,self-hosted
created_at: "2026-07-11T13:27:36.450Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-12T16:00:42.612Z"
closed_at: "2026-07-11T13:43:13.010Z"
author: codex
acceptance_criteria: OIDC is disabled by default; partial production configuration fails closed; discovery/JWKS and exact token validation are used; identity resolution is transactional and safe; password login remains; generic docs and tests pass with no hosted values.
risk: high
confidence: high
resolution: "Public pm-web now supports reusable self-hosted OIDC using only generic OIDC_* configuration; full typecheck, tests, build, npm audit, and diff checks pass."
expected_result: "Optional generic OIDC login is disabled by default, fails closed on partial production config, securely validates protocol state and identity, preserves password login, and adds no hosted values."
actual_result: "Implemented openid-client discovery/JWKS Authorization Code + PKCE, signed state cookies, exact claim checks, transactional issuer-subject mapping, verified-email collision rules, OIDC-only provisioning, UI discovery, schema, docs, and 12 focused OIDC tests within a 60-test passing suite."
notes[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-11T13:40:13.068Z",codex,"Implemented optional provider-neutral OIDC Authorization Code + PKCE S256 login. Environment contract: OIDC_ISSUER, OIDC_CLIENT_ID, OIDC_CLIENT_SECRET, OIDC_REDIRECT_URI, optional OIDC_SCOPES (default openid profile email), dedicated OIDC_COOKIE_SECRET, and optional OIDC_REQUIRE_VERIFIED_EMAIL. OIDC remains disabled with no variables and partial production configuration stops startup."
  "2026-07-12T14:56:24.090Z",codex,"Pre-push Greptile d40def06 found root issuer normalization, advisory-lock ordering clarity, and callback observability issues. Root issuers now canonicalize to URL.origin with a regression test; shared-email locking occurs before mapping lookup; non-protocol callback errors log only a safe error class/code. Full gate passes with 67 tests."
  "2026-07-12T16:00:42.607Z",codex,"2026-07-12 final bot-review correction: enforced the platform-wide HTML hidden contract with `[hidden] { display: none !important; }` so component display classes cannot expose disabled OIDC controls; added a regression assertion in test/oidc.test.ts. Full 68-test suite, typecheck, and build pass."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-11T13:40:13.602Z",codex,"Use immutable issuer+subject as the external identity key. Email may link an existing account only when email_verified is the boolean true; unverified collisions must be rejected. Provider discovery/JWKS and code-grant validation stay in openid-client, with explicit defense-in-depth issuer, audience, nonce, and time checks."
